<title>USA: Fairchild gets option to buy Simmonds stake.</title>
<headline>Fairchild gets option to buy Simmonds stake.</headline>
<dateline>CHANTILLY, Va. 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Fairchild Corp said its fasteners unit has acquired an exclusive option to buy a majority stake in Simmonds SA, a European maker of aerospace fasteners, from  Mines de Kali Sainte-Therese.</p>
<p>The purchase of the 84.2 percent stake of Simmonds on a fully diluted basis would total $21 million, plus the assumption of $35.5 million in debt, Fairchild said in a statement Thursday.</p>
<p>The transaction, which is contingent upon the completion of due diligence and necessary approvals, calls for Fairchild to purchase Simmonds common shares and convertible notes, the company said.</p>
</text>
